<title>UK: BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 18.</title>
<headline>BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 18.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the election diary for Friday April 18:</p>
<p>Prime Minister John Major, Deputy Prime Minister Michael Heseltine, Trade and Industry Secretary Ian Lang and Conservative Party chairman Brian Mawhinney present daily news briefing at 9.15 a.m. (0815 GMT)</p>
<p>Major then sets off on campaign trail to northern England</p>
<p>Labour Party Shadow Chancellor Gordon Brown and Shadow Home Secretary Jack Straw present daily news briefing at 8.30 a.m. (0730 GMT)</p>
<p>Labour leader Tony Blair has no public appearances planned.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +4471 542 7950</p>
